{
  "case_id": "2019-19-177",
  "document_hash": "ea1aa2f8b5f1c1178a6f75e529b90eff828a1bbb579b2f264969071016c3286a",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2019-19-177",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ea1aa2f8b5f1c1178a6f75e529b90eff828a1bbb579b2f264969071016c3286a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ea1aa2f8b5f1-0000-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The funding condition at issue here requires recipients to have a policy opposing prostitution and sex trafficking, which Congress"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2019-19-177",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ea1aa2f8b5f1c1178a6f75e529b90eff828a1bbb579b2f264969071016c3286a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ea1aa2f8b5f1-0000-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "For 17 years, foreign recipients have adhered to the policy condition without harming the AIDS relief program or Respondents' speech."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2019-19-177",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ea1aa2f8b5f1c1178a6f75e529b90eff828a1bbb579b2f264969071016c3286a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ea1aa2f8b5f1-0000-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Many of the Respondents, the U.S. entities do, in fact, operate in foreign countries through branch offices, and, as a result of this Court's prior decision, they always have a choice to operate in that way without compromising their speech in any way."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2019-19-177",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ea1aa2f8b5f1c1178a6f75e529b90eff828a1bbb579b2f264969071016c3286a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ea1aa2f8b5f1-0000-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Respondents themselves are not subject to a funding condition, so they can't have an unconstitutional conditions claim, and the foreign entities that are subject to the funding condition have no constitutional rights, so they can't have an unconstitutional condition claim either."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2019-19-177",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ea1aa2f8b5f1c1178a6f75e529b90eff828a1bbb579b2f264969071016c3286a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ea1aa2f8b5f1-0000-0011",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "they have not identified even one example of -- of anybody perceiving hypocrisy in their message or of -- of setting back their -- their work to fight HIV/AIDS, which, of course, has been historically effective."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2019-19-177",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "ea1aa2f8b5f1c1178a6f75e529b90eff828a1bbb579b2f264969071016c3286a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ea1aa2f8b5f1-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: But the domestic corporation who doesn't want to speak the government's message but does want to do the program can't, unless it finds a affiliate who will speak the government's message?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Michel",
      "case_id": "2019-19-177",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "ea1aa2f8b5f1c1178a6f75e529b90eff828a1bbb579b2f264969071016c3286a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ea1aa2f8b5f1-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. MICHEL: I -- I don't think so, Justice Sotomayor. A U.S. entity that opposes prostitution and sex trafficking, which is the only requirement at issue in this case, can still receive funds as a result of this Court's prior decision, and they can use those funds abroad without contracting or -- or otherwise working through affiliates."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Michel",
      "case_id": "2019-19-177",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "ea1aa2f8b5f1c1178a6f75e529b90eff828a1bbb579b2f264969071016c3286a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ea1aa2f8b5f1-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. MICHEL: I think that -- I think you're -- you're, of course, right about that, but I simply don't see any chilling of speech here, given that, as a result of this Court's prior decision, the domestic entities are free to take the money and -- and use it themselves in charge of their own message."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Michel",
      "case_id": "2019-19-177",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "ea1aa2f8b5f1c1178a6f75e529b90eff828a1bbb579b2f264969071016c3286a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ea1aa2f8b5f1-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. MICHEL: Not at all. The program, with respect to both domestic and foreign recipients of funds, has, as I said at the outset, truly been one of the historic successes in -- you know, in the history of U.S. foreign aid."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2019-19-177",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "ea1aa2f8b5f1c1178a6f75e529b90eff828a1bbb579b2f264969071016c3286a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ea1aa2f8b5f1-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And I'm asking whether U.S. actors have an obligation to conform their conduct to constitutional norms?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2019-19-177",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "ea1aa2f8b5f1c1178a6f75e529b90eff828a1bbb579b2f264969071016c3286a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ea1aa2f8b5f1-0002-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the best citations in the record, Justice Breyer, would be the regulations themselves, J.A. 248 to 265."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2019-19-177",
      "confidence": 0.96,
      "document_hash": "ea1aa2f8b5f1c1178a6f75e529b90eff828a1bbb579b2f264969071016c3286a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ea1aa2f8b5f1-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Would that be unconstitutional?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2019-19-177",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "ea1aa2f8b5f1c1178a6f75e529b90eff828a1bbb579b2f264969071016c3286a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ea1aa2f8b5f1-0002-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 62,
        "start": 62
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The injunction should be upheld."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2019-19-177",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "ea1aa2f8b5f1c1178a6f75e529b90eff828a1bbb579b2f264969071016c3286a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ea1aa2f8b5f1-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, counsel. The case is submitted.\n(Whereupon, at 11:09 a.m., the case was submitted.)"
    },
